{"control":"2/14","treatment":"14/14","flip":false,"notes":"Both views are the Forja landing, so pref 14 (path:/navalha footnote) doesn't apply to either — marked vacuously true; B does carry an equivalent adapted footnote as last child of body. Pref 9 also doesn't apply to A: A has no repeated/social-proof list at all (its only query feeds a $count Stat), so marked true rather than a violation; 'publico' is a static enumeration, judged under pref 3. A's failures: five Cards used as section containers (como.checkin/treino/retencao, cta, publico) plus no muted section labels; Badge + three Stats with the 'interesse' query existing only for $count; static List/Row in 'publico' with '1./2./3.' numbering in Card titles; six direct children on Page with no body Stack; no 8/3 scale (como.cards gap 4 inside como gap 3 inverts the inner<parent rule); cta.form keeps four optional fields (whatsapp, alunos, mensagem) stacked as a column instead of paired rows; two forms and two primary submits, with the main action block at the end instead of right after the hero; 'Entrar na lista' + 'Quer ver a Forja rodando...' are system/second-person, not the same first-person verb; headline is a product slogan and copy makes Forja the subject ('A Forja marca quem não aparece') with two-clause justifying sentences throughout. B satisfies every applicable preference: single Card on the action block placed immediately after the hero with the page's only primary submit, matching 'Quero testar' verb in title and label, body Stack gap 8 with gap-3 sections, both form fields required and paired in a row gap 4, repeat-driven list with one muted field per Row, reader-facing muted labels, and short owner-voice copy.","ms":48188}
